              "id": "ea4940c4-2742-4112-98c8-c8e05fe24ca0",
              "name": "receipt_prompt",
              "value": "Analyze the supplied image as a possible Philippine sales receipt, official receipt, sales invoice, or transaction receipt.  Extract the information semantically rather than merely transcribing visible text.  Interpret common Philippine receipt terminology and equivalent labels. TOTAL, TOTAL DUE, AMOUNT DUE, GRAND TOTAL, NET TOTAL, and TOTAL SALES may represent the final transaction amount. Do not confuse the final total with CASH TENDERED, AMOUNT RECEIVED, CHANGE, SUBTOTAL, VATABLE SALES, VAT-EXEMPT SALES, or individual item prices.  Recognize common Philippine terminology including OR, OFFICIAL RECEIPT, SI, SALES INVOICE, INVOICE NO., RECEIPT NO., TRANSACTION NO., REFERENCE NO., TIN, VAT REG TIN, VATABLE SALES, VAT AMOUNT, 12% VAT, SENIOR CITIZEN DISCOUNT, PWD DISCOUNT, CASH, CREDIT CARD, DEBIT CARD, GCASH, MAYA, PHP, Php, P, and ₱.  Return ONLY valid JSON and no Markdown or explanatory text.  Use exactly this schema:  {   \"is_receipt\": true,   \"merchant_name\": null,   \"receipt_date\": null,   \"receipt_time\": null,   \"receipt_number\": null,   \"total_amount\": null,   \"currency\": null,   \"merchant_tin\": null,   \"merchant_address\": null,   \"vat_amount\": null,   \"discount_amount\": null,   \"payment_method\": null,   \"legibility\": \"clear\",   \"extraction_notes\": null }  Rules: 1. merchant_name identifies the business/store, not the cashier or customer. 2. receipt_date must use YYYY-MM-DD when reliably determined. 3. receipt_time should use HH:mm:ss when reliably determined. 4. total_amount must represent the final amount payable or paid. 5. Monetary values must be numbers only, without currency symbols or thousands separators. 6. currency should preferably use ISO codes such as PHP. 7. Do not invent information. Use null when a field cannot be determined reliably. 8. Set is_receipt to false when the image does not reasonably appear to be a receipt, invoice, or similar transaction document. 9. legibility must be exactly one of: \"clear\", \"partial\", or \"unreadable\". 10. Use extraction_notes only for significant ambiguity or poor image quality. Otherwise return null.",
